            if (nums[i] == candidate) {
                found = 1;
                break;
            }
        }

        // If candidate not found → return it
        if (!found) {
            return candidate;
        }
    }

    // This line will never be hit because loop always returns
    return numsSize + 1;
}
```

---

### 🔹 Why this now passes
- Example `nums = [7,8,9,11,12]`  
  - Check `1`: not found → return `1`. ✅  
- Example `nums = [1,2,0]`  
  - `1` found, `2` found, `3` not found → return `3`. ✅  
- Example `nums = [3,4,-1,1]`  
  - `1` found, `2` not found → return `2`. ✅  

---

